# Reverse away from a surface, far enough that whatever happens next does not drag the arm across
# it.
#
# It reverses and stops. It does not turn, and it does not walk anywhere: a navigation goal
# normally follows, and Nav2 is far better at going somewhere than a hand-rolled pulse controller.
# The only job here is to get the base clear.
#
# Reverse is real, but only just: the policy measures -0.247 m/s for a commanded -0.60 and exactly
# 0.000 for -0.40, and g1_gait_shaper has a separate rev_engage above a planner's backup speeds so
# a deliberate command like this one gets through.

# How far to end up from where it started, in metres. Achieved to within about one gait pulse.
float64 distance_m
# Give up after this many seconds. 0 uses the server's own default.
float64 timeout_s
---
bool success
string message
float64 travelled_m
---
string PHASE_BACKING_OFF=backing_off
string phase
float64 travelled_m
